  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform chain of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> overhangs a smooth table with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;laying on the table. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is the kinetic energy of the chain in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> as it completely slips off the table, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Take&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "40",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0098_74ea1886acba.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 208px;\" /></p><p>Apply conservation of energy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>KE</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>K.E.</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>K.E.</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
  }
